.TH GIT-STACK 1 "" "" "Git Stack Manual"
.SH NAME
git-stack \- manage a stack of branches encoded as git notes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git stack
.I command
.RI [ args ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git stack
manages a stack of branches encoded as git notes on the commits in the
range
.IR @{u}..HEAD .
Each commit may be linked to one or more branch names; the subcommands
build, push, and prune those branches from the linked commits.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sync
Cherry-pick each commit onto its noted branch(es), rebuilding each branch
from
.IR @{u} .
Stashes the working tree first and prompts for confirmation.
.TP
.B rebase
Run an interactive autosquash rebase onto
.IR @{u} ,
applying any
.B --fixup
or
.B --squash
commits. Stashes first and prompts for confirmation.
.TP
.B push
Force-push
.RB ( "git push -fu origin" )
each branch named in the stack's commit notes. Branches with no diff
against their remote are skipped.
.TP
.B clean
Delete local stack branches that are no longer referenced by any commit
note. Lists the branches and prompts for confirmation.
.TP
.B log
Pretty-print the commits in
.I @{u}..HEAD
along with each commit's branch notes.
.TP
.BI "link " "branch spec..."
Link the resolved commit(s) to
.IR branch .
Each
.I spec
is a single commit or a range
.RI ( a..b ).
A commit may be linked to multiple branches.
.TP
.BI "unlink " "branch spec..."
Unlink the resolved commit(s) from
.IR branch .
The note is deleted when its last branch is removed.
.TP
.BR help ", " --help ", " -h
Show usage. Note that
.B git stack --help
is intercepted by git itself (rewritten to a manpage lookup); use
.B git stack help
or
.B git-stack --help
to reach the script's own handler.
.SH NOTES
Branch membership is stored in
.I refs/notes/commits
and in per-branch refs under
.IR refs/git-stack/ .
A repository lock
.RI ( git-stack.lock
in the git dir) serializes mutating operations.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-notes (1),
.BR git-rebase (1)
